{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1531235-question-about-fetters","id":1531235,"title":"Question about fetters","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-21T09:43:29-08:00","id":1531235,"title":"Question about fetters","content":"Does a wraith know what their fetters are and where they are? Can they travel between fetters without Argos quickly or do they have to do so mundanely if they don\u2019t have Argos?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2818-frostfox","name":"FrostFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-21T11:57:24-08:00","id":1531240,"title":"","content":"The default assumption appears to be that a wraith knows what their Fetters are, if not necessarily why they're Fetters. Normally, assuming the Fetter's not in a fixed location, they have to go looking for it; the Lifeweb art Sense Strands gives them constant awareness of their Fetters' locations.<br /> <br /> Travel to a Fetter without Argos is usually mundane, unless they have the 4-dot Lifeweb initiate art Walk the Web, which lets them cut down travel time to a Fetter, from anywhere from an hour to a turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}